From: ESP32-S31 Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: reject unsafe Xesploop control flow

The XEspressif hardware loop state cannot be cancelled when control flow
leaves the loop body before its configured end address.  Converting a loop
that contains a return, break, or other outgoing edge therefore leaves the
hardware loop armed and can corrupt subsequent control flow.

The generic hw-doloop analysis already records this condition as
jumps_outof.  Reject these loops in the RISC-V target hook so that GCC falls
back to an ordinary branch loop while retaining Xesploop for single-exit
loops.

The XEspressif TRM also warns that placing a branch or jump at the hardware
loop end address can cause unexpected behavior.  A label-only latch can alias
the HWLP end address with a branch in the successor block, so materialize a
nop at that boundary and reject an actual jump latch.
---
 gcc/config/riscv/riscv.cc | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/riscv/riscv.cc b/gcc/config/riscv/riscv.cc
--- a/gcc/config/riscv/riscv.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/riscv/riscv.cc
@@ -14367,7 +14367,10 @@ riscv_hwloops_opt_p (hwloop_info loop)
   if (loop->depth > 2)
     return false;
 
-  if (loop->has_call || loop->has_asm)
+  /* XEspressif hardware loops cannot be cancelled on an early exit.  If a
+     branch leaves the loop body, the loop state remains armed and can alter
+     control flow after the branch target (including after a return).  */
+  if (loop->has_call || loop->has_asm || loop->jumps_outof)
     return false;
 
   if (!loop->incoming_dest || loop->incoming_dest != loop->head)
@@ -14390,2 +14393,9 @@ riscv_hwloops_opt_p (hwloop_info loop)
-  if (!last_insn)
+  /* The XEspressif TRM warns that a branch or jump at the HWLP end address
+     can cause unexpected behavior.  A label-only latch otherwise aliases the
+     end address with the first instruction in the successor block, so give
+     it a real nop.  Reject an actual jump latch.  */
+  if (!last_insn)
     return false;
+  bool label_latch = LABEL_P (last_insn);
+  if (JUMP_P (last_insn))
+    return false;
@@ -14394,3 +14405,5 @@ riscv_hwloops_opt_p (hwloop_info loop)
   rtx_code_label *end_label = gen_label_rtx ();
   emit_label_before (end_label, last_insn);
+  if (label_latch)
+    emit_insn_after (gen_nop (), last_insn);
 
-- 
2.39.5

